T*
(            Healthcare Management System Automation Framework PROJECT DOCUMENTATION Java |) Tj
T*
(            Selenium WebDriver | Cucumber BDD | JUnit | Maven | Jenkins | GitHub 1. Project) Tj
T*
(            Overview The Healthcare Management System Automation Framework is an end-to-end UI) Tj
T*
(            test automation project for important workflows in a healthcare management) Tj
T*
(            application. It uses Java and Selenium WebDriver for browser automation, Cucumber) Tj
T*
(            BDD for readable scenarios, JUnit for test execution, and Maven for build and) Tj
T*
(            dependency management. Jenkins is integrated with the GitHub repository. A code) Tj
T*
(            change was pushed and a new Jenkins build was observed. The test target is a locally) Tj
T*
(            hosted healthcare demo application called CarePoint. Objectives - Automate) Tj
T*
(            healthcare application workflows. - Validate authentication and user access. - Test) Tj
T*
(            patient registration and appointment management. - Build reusable automation) Tj
T*
(            components. - Generate readable test reports. - Integrate test execution with CI. 2.) Tj
T*
(            Technology Stack Technology Purpose Java 17 Automation programming language Selenium) Tj
T*
(            WebDriver 4.25.0 Browser automation Cucumber 7.20.1 Behaviour-Driven Development) Tj
T*
(            JUnit 4.13.2 Test execution Maven 3.10.0 Build and dependency management Jenkins) Tj
T*
(            2.589 Continuous Integration Git and GitHub Version control and source repository) Tj
T*
(            GitHub Webhooks Build triggering HTML Publisher Publishing HTML reports Runtime) Tj
T*
(            note: the automation project uses Java 17; Jenkins itself runs using Java 21. These) Tj
T*
(            are separate runtime configurations. 3. Project Architecture The framework follows a) Tj
T*
(            layered structure based on the Page Object Model \(POM\).Healthcare Management System) Tj
T*
(            Automation Framework Page 1) Tj
T*
ET
