(Healthcare Management System Automation Framework) Tj
T*
(Project Documentation - Page 4 of 5) Tj
T*
T*
( Troubleshooting achievement Cucumber reports were initially generated in the local project) Tj
T*
( directory while HTML Publisher searched in the Jenkins workspace. This caused publishing to) Tj
T*
( fail despite successful test execution. The build script was updated to copy HTML, JSON and XML) Tj
T*
( reports into %WORKSPACE%\\reports before publishing. This resolved the directory mismatch. 10.) Tj
T*
( Cucumber Reporting The Cucumber runner generates console output and HTML, JSON and JUnit XML) Tj
T*
( reports. plugin = { "pretty", "html:reports/cucumber.html", "json:reports/cucumber.json",) Tj
T*
( "junit:reports/cucumber.xml" } - HTML: human-readable scenario and feature results. - JSON:) Tj
T*
( structured results for downstream reporting integrations. - XML: JUnit-compatible results for) Tj
T*
( CI integrations. The HTML report is copied to index.html in the Jenkins workspace for) Tj
T*
( publication. 11. GitHub and Automatic Build Triggering The project was initialized as a Git) Tj
T*
( repository, committed and pushed to GitHub:) Tj
T*
( https://github.com/hrts51/healthcare-automation-framework git init git add . git commit -m) Tj
T*
( "Initial commit - Healthcare Automation Framework" git branch -M main git remote add origin) Tj
T*
( https://github.com/hrts51/healthcare-automation-framework.git git push -u origin main Jenkins) Tj
T*
( was configured with the repository URL, branch specifier */main, and GitHub hook trigger for) Tj
T*
( GITScm polling. A README change was committed and pushed; a new Jenkins build appeared without) Tj
T*
( manually selecting Build Now. Verification caveat: the GitHub webhook page previously displayed) Tj
T*
( a connection warning for a placeholder public URL. The observed automatic build confirms that a) Tj
T*
( trigger path worked, but the exact webhook delivery configuration should still be checked) Tj
T*
( before claiming every delivery is successful. 12. What Makes This Implementation Stand Out?) Tj
T*
( Project-specific differentiators - Healthcare-oriented workflows rather than only a generic) Tj
T*
( login demonstration. - A locally hosted CarePoint demo application used as a controllable test) Tj
T*
( target. - Separate Java runtimes: Java 17 for the test project and Java 21 for Jenkins. - A) Tj
T*
( practical Jenkins workspace/report-directory mismatch diagnosed and fixed by copying report) Tj
T*
( files before publication. - An integrated GitHub-to-Jenkins workflow where a repository change) Tj
T*
( was followed by a new Jenkins build. - Multiple report formats-HTML, JSON and XML-from the same) Tj
T*
( Cucumber execution. - Separate local ports: CarePoint on 8080 and Jenkins on 8081. These are) Tj
T*
( implementation differentiators, not claims that the underlying technologies or techniques are) Tj
T*
( globally unique. The value is in combining and troubleshooting them into a working project. 13.) Tj
T*
( Known Limitations and Accuracy Notes - The target is a local demo application, not a real) Tj
T*
( healthcare provider system. - The current suite contains six scenarios and should be expanded.) Tj
T*
( - The local application server must be running for UI tests. - The Jenkins job currently) Tj
T*
( depends on a local project directory. - The webhook delivery configuration should be) Tj
T*
( verified.Healthcare Management System Automation Framework Page 4) Tj
T*
ET
